// 011 — Print environment variables — DESIGN NOTE
// On Linux, the environment is `char **environ` — a NULL-terminated
// array of "KEY=VALUE" strings the kernel hands you at exec time.
// `getenv("KEY")` walks that array to find a match.
//
// AiLang doesn't yet ship a GetEnv() wrapper; the canonical
// `Library.OS.Linux` userspace surface is on the roadmap (see the
// session notes about the linux compatibility library). When it
// lands, this demo will read PATH and HOME via Env_Get(name).
//
// In the meantime: the environ pointer is reachable through
// SystemCall + raw memory walks, but a one-liner GetEnv is missing.
SubRoutine.Main {
    PrintMessage("(env access waits on Library.OS.Linux Env_Get(name))\n")
    PrintMessage("planned: Env_Get(\"HOME\") -> Address (NULL if unset)\n")
}
RunTask(Main)
